  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing conflict-sensitive approaches: training Korean stakeholders in conflict and fragile environments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM and the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) maintain a strong and ongoing partnership in supporting development interventions in fragile and conflict-affected settings. This collaboration is reflected in joint initiatives that integrate conflict-sensitive approaches into programming, drawing on IOM&apos;s operational expertise and KOICA&apos;s expanding role as a development actor. The project is designed to enhance the capacity of stakeholders engaged in KOICA Conflict and Fragility Programme by delivering a focused training on Conflict Sensitivity and Conflict Analysis and the application of conflict-sensitive approaches.</narrative>
  </description>
